 the provincial capital, is planning to become the first provincial capital in the world to relocate because of sea-level rise. The regional average conceals this: land can vanish completely in one province while the wider region gains.","facts":[["Islands lost entirely","5 \u2014 Kakatina, Kale, Rapita, Rehana, Zollies"],["Nuatambu","25 families; 11 houses lost since 2011"],["Nuatambu habitable land lost","more than half"],["Taro","first provincial capital worldwide planning relocation"]],"sources":[["Albert et al. 2016, Environmental Research Letters \u2014 33 islands, imagery 1947\u20132014","https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/1748-9326/11/5/054011"],["Rising sea levels blamed for the disappearance of five reef islands \u2014 ABC News","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2016-05-07/rising-sea-levels-blamed-for-wiping-out-five-islands/7392986"],["Five Pacific islands have already disappeared \u2014 Mongabay","https://news.mongabay.com/2016/05/five-pacific-islands-already-disappeared-due-sea-level-rise/"]]},"geo":"SB","territory":"Solomon Islands","sea_level_mm_yr":5.1,"sst_warming_c":0.84,"sea_level_series":[[1993,-0.1],[1994,0.0],[1995,0.0],[1996,0.1],[1997,0.0],[1998,-0.1],[1999,0.0],[2000,0.1],[2001,0.1],[2002,0.0],[2003,0.0],[2004,0.0],[2005,0.0],[2006,0.0],[2007,0.1],[2008,0.1],[2009,0.1],[2010,0.0],[2011,0.1],[2012,0.1],[2013,0.1],[2014,0.1],[2015,0.0],[2016,0.0],[2017,0.1],[2018,0.1],[2019,0.1],[2020,0.1],[2021,0.2],[2022,0.2],[2023,0.1]],"traj":[{"y":1999,"d":-2.99,"n":204},{"y":2001,"d":4321.75,"n":18},{"y":2002,"d":4322.52,"n":18},{"y":2003,"d":-4790.83,"n":5},{"y":2004,"d":928.75,"n":92},{"y":2005,"d":0.52,"n":204},{"y":2006,"d":1.29,"n":204},{"y":2007,"d":1046.49,"n":171},{"y":2008,"d":3205.12,"n":27},{"y":2009,"d":1.43,"n":204},{"y":2010,"d":-80.63,"n":171},{"y":2011,"d":-1.07,"n":204},{"y":2012,"d":0.81,"n":204},{"y":2013,"d":3.66,"n":204},{"y":2014,"d":4.62,"n":204},{"y":2015,"d":1.65,"n":204},{"y":2016,"d":0.38,"n":204},{"y":2017,"d":0.1,"n":204},