,2023],"relocation":{"status":"staying","headline":"The emblem of the drowning Pacific is gaining land.","body":"Funafuti is the image the world uses for a nation going under. Across 1,385 quality-controlled transects the median shoreline is advancing at 0.21 metres a year, and independent research has found Tuvalu's land area grew over recent decades. This is not a reprieve. A reef island keeps its area by rebuilding from coral debris and by moving \u2014 the sand goes somewhere new. Groundwater still salts up, king tides still flood the runway, and a house cannot rebuild itself the way a beach can.","facts":[["Median shoreline change","+0.21 m/yr"],["Transects measured","1,385 (769 statistically significant)"],["Transects eroding","33.9%"]],"sources":[]},"geo":"TV","territory":"Tuvalu","sea_level_mm_yr":4.4,"sst_warming_c":0.78,"sea_level_series":[[1993,0.0],[1994,0.0],[1995,0.0],[1996,0.0],[1997,0.0],[1998,-0.2],[1999,0.0],[2000,0.0],[2001,0.0],[2002,0.1],[2003,0.0],[2004,0.1],[2005,0.1],[2006,0.1],[2007,0.1],[2008,0.1],[2009,0.0],[2010,0.0],[2011,0.1],[2012,0.0],[2013,0.1],[2014,0.1],[2015,0.1],[2016,0.0],[2017,0.1],[2018,0.1],[2019,0.1],[2020,0.1],[2021,0.1],[2022,0.1],[2023,0.1]],"traj":[{"y":1999,"d":-8.0,"n":1352},{"y":2000,"d":-11.65,"n":1352},{"y":2001,"d":-8.32,"n":1385},{"y":2003,"d":-10.77,"n":1385},{"y":2004,"d":-7.46,"n":1385},{"y":2006,"d":-2.08,"n":1385},{"y":2007,"d":-1.33,"n":1305},{"y":2008,"d":0.53,"n":1303},{"y":2009,"d":2.96,"n":1385},{"y":2010,"d":-0.78,"n":1010},{"y":2011,"d":-4.87,"n":1385},{"y":2012,"d":-2.88,"n":1385},{"y":2013,"d":-1.36,"n":1385},{"y":2014,"d":-1.18,"n":1385},{"y":2015,"d":-0.97,"n":1385},{"y":2016,"d":1.09,"n":1385},{"y":2017,"d":0.42,"n":1385},{"y":2018,"d":-0.85,"n":1385},{"y":2019,"d":0.11,"n":1385},{"y":2020,"d":-0.42,"n":1385},{"y":2021,"d":-0.22,"n":1385},{"y":2022,"d":-0.3,"n":1385},{"y":2023,"d":0.0,"n":1385}]},{"site":"carteret","label":"Carteret Islands","country":"Papua New Guinea","group":"Melanesia","n_good":251,"n_sig":36,"pct_sig":14.3,"median_rate_m_yr":0.334,"mean_rate_m_yr":0.342,"median_sig_rate_m_yr":0.783,"pct_eroding":23.1,"pct_sig_eroding":0.0,"median_sce_m":51.5,"p90_sce_m":82.0,"median_net_m":8.3,"churn_ratio":6.2,"rate_p10":-0.19,"rate_p90":0.8,"median_valid_span_yr":25,"has_transects":true,"has_shorelines":true,"years":[2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023],"relocation":{"status":"relocating","headline":"Its people are leaving. Its shoreline is gaining land.","body":"Around 1,700 Carteret Islanders are being moved to mainland Bougainville by Tulele Peisa, the community organisation founded by Ursula Rakova. An earlier government resettlement moved 10 families in 1984; they returned by 1989. The Catholic Church provided 25 hectares at Tinputz, enough for about 100 people, with further land at Tearouki and Mabiri. In 2022 the programme was seeking K14 million to move 350 families by 2027. The islanders are not leaving because the land disappeared. They are leaving because saltwater ruined the gardens and the wells.","facts":[["People to be relocated","~1,700"],["Families targeted by 2027","350"],["First attempt","1984 \u2014 10 families, returned by 1989"],["Destination","Tinputz, Tearouki, Mabiri (Bougainville)"]],"sources":[["Carteret Island needs K14 million to move 350 families by 2027 \u2014 PINA, 2022","https://pina.com.fj/2022/11/24/carteret-island-needs-k14-million-to-move-350-families-by-2027/"],["Carteret Island climate refugees make a new home \u2014 ReliefWeb","https://reliefweb.int/report/papua-new-guinea/carteret-island-climate-refugees-make-new-home"],["Strengthening Our Ancestral Community Across the Seas \u2014 Cultural Survival","https://www.culturalsurvival.org/publications/cultural-survival-quarterly/strengthening-our-ancestral-community-across-seas"]]},"geo":"PG","territory":"Papua New Guinea","sea_level_mm_yr":5.4,"sst_warming_c":0.81,"sea_level_series":[[1993,-0.1],[1994,0.0],[1995,0.0],[1996,0.0],[1997,0.